{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21ed7e39d99b57bc5ad7", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Electrostatics - Test 8", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 40, "totalQuestions": 20, "totalMarks": 80, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 80, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 20, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a86b2"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a86af", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8647", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae6"], "topics": ["60ced3320e34b73944ddfaa5"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e4d"], "question": {"text": "<p>A point charge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> vertically above the centre of a square of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> as shown in figure. The magnitude of the electric flux through the square will be _______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F9913bae1-f549-4860-846f-b350587deedf-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 122px; height: 160px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "4d745a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8648"}, {"id": "e7afc5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8649"}, {"id": "43eb26", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a864a"}, {"id": "735840", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a864b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a864c", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae6"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4753"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4703"], "question": {"text": "<p>As shown in the figure, a configuration of two equal point charges <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is placed on an inclined plane. Mass of each point charge is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>. Assume that there is no friction between charge and plane. For the system of two point charges to be in equilibrium (at rest) the height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The value of<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mtext>&#160;Take&#160;</mtext><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F1c41f125-c078-4d15-a66c-46c2ba6a0c57-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 167px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "efecd4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a864d"}, {"id": "ed5a5f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a864e"}, {"id": "b355ab", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a864f"}, {"id": "7b4838", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8650"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8651", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae6"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b59"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b29"], "question": {"text": "An infinite plane sheet of charge having uniform surface charge density $+\\sigma_s \\mathrm{C} / \\mathrm{m}^2$ is placed on $x-y$ plane. Another infinitely long line charge having uniform linear charge density $+\\lambda_e \\mathrm{C} / \\mathrm{m}$ is placed at $z=4 \\mathrm{~m}$ plane and parallel to $y$-axis. If the magnitude values $\\left|\\sigma_{\\mathrm{s}}\\right|=2\\left|\\lambda_{\\mathrm{e}}\\right|$ then at point $(0,0,2)$, the ratio of magnitudes of electric field values due to sheet charge to that of line charge is $\\pi \\sqrt{n}: 1$. The value of $n$ is_______."}, "options": [{"id": "ff050a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8652"}, {"id": "33c138", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8653"}, {"id": "c586a5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8654"}, {"id": "24c020", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8655"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8656", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae6"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4762"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4718"], "question": {"text": "<p>For a charged spherical ball, electrostatic potential inside the ball varies with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>.</p><p>Here, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> are constant and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> is the distance from the center. The volume charge density inside the ball is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>&#949;</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math> is ______.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#949;</mi><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;permittivity of medium.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "5d699a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8657"}, {"id": "33e23a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8658"}, {"id": "5e08f8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8659"}, {"id": "c1a957", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a865a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a865b", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae6"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b59"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8ed5"], "question": {"text": "If the net electric field at point $\\mathrm{P}$ along $\\mathrm{Y}$ axis is zero, then the ratio of $\\left|\\frac{q_2}{q_3}\\right|$ is $\\frac{8}{5 \\sqrt{x}}$, where $x=$ _____.\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FTENXZqdWoZtzBsZzXo4X7z8-7UakOtjMlAyt617tVwQ.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "c3ee1c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a865c"}, {"id": "2e5c55", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a865d"}, {"id": "9c9b17", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a865e"}, {"id": "545adb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a865f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8660", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae6"], "topics": ["60ced3320e34b73944ddfaa5"], "concepts": ["6117b9b767dbe2603c3ea7cd"], "question": {"text": "The total charge enclosed in an incremental volume of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></math> located at the origin is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><menclose notation=\"bottom\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></menclose></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>nC</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;if electric flux density of its field is found as<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mi>sin</mi><mi>y</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mi>cosy</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "ce62e8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8661"}, {"id": "dc9da8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8662"}, {"id": "67d196", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8663"}, {"id": "51bc30", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8664"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8665", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae6"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4753"], "concepts": ["6117b9d167dbe2603c3eacc8"], "question": {"text": "Two identical charged spheres are suspended by strings of equal lengths. The string make an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>37</mn><mo>°</mo></math> with each other. When suspended in a liquid of density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>, the angle remains same. If density of material of the sphere is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>, the dielectric constant of the liquid is _____ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mn>37</mn><mo>°</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "6afa29", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8666"}, {"id": "fc6ec4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8667"}, {"id": "385054", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8668"}, {"id": "532858", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8669"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a866a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae6"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4762"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4718"], "question": {"text": "Three concentric spherical metallic shells <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Y</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi></math> of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math> respectively&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> have surface charge densities <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#963;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#963;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#963;</mi></math>, respectively. The shells <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi></math> are at same potential. If the radii of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Y</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, respectively. The radius of shell <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi></math> is _____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "b06e66", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a866b"}, {"id": "41de1c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a866c"}, {"id": "c7088d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a866d"}, {"id": "96f25d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a866e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a866f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae6"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b59"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b12"], "question": {"text": "A stream of a positively charged particles having <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">q</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">m</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>11</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>kg</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is deflected by an electric field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">^</mo></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kV</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The electric field exists in a region of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> along <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> direction. Due to the electric field, the deflection of the charge particles in the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math> direction is _____&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mm</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "93c67f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8670"}, {"id": "ee353f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8671"}, {"id": "eab79b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8672"}, {"id": "e89bc3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8673"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8674", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae6"], "topics": ["60ced3320e34b73944ddfaa5"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e4d"], "question": {"text": "The electric field in a region is given by $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{E}}=(2 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+4 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+6 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}}) \\times 10^3 \\mathrm{~N} / \\mathrm{C}$. The flux of the field through a rectangular surface parallel to $x-z$ plane is $6.0 \\mathrm{Nm}^2 \\mathrm{C}^{-1}$. The area of the surface is ________ $\\mathrm{cm}^2$."}, "options": [{"id": "815154", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8675"}, {"id": "f6d6d8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8676"}, {"id": "b957a8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8677"}, {"id": "fed843", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8678"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8679", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae6"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4753"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4703"], "question": {"text": "<p>An infinite number of point charges, each&nbsp;carrying <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> charge, are placed along the y-axis at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>The total force on a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> point charge, placed at the origin, is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>,&nbsp;to&nbsp;the nearest integer, is ___ .</p><p>[Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>]</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "c60034", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a867a"}, {"id": "286d69", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a867b"}, {"id": "bf438e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a867c"}, {"id": "362322", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a867d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a867e", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae6"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b59"], "concepts": ["6162fb196ed13040ec84b0c4"], "question": {"text": "<p>A cubical volume is bounded by the surfaces <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math>. The electric field in the region is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">E</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>x</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">i</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">^</mo></mover></math>. Where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>NC</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, the charge contained in the cubical volume is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> is ______.</p><p>(Take&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "64e68c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a867f"}, {"id": "1deea0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8680"}, {"id": "a99c87", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8681"}, {"id": "ebd2a8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8682"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8683", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae6"], "topics": ["60ced3320e34b73944ddfaa5"], "concepts": ["6117b9b767dbe2603c3ea7cd"], "question": {"text": "<p>As shown in figure, a cuboid lies in a region with electric field&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">^</mo></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.&nbsp;The magnitude of charge within the cuboid is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>.</p><p>The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> is ______&nbsp;(if dimension of cuboid is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>)</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F874752b9-d8ea-4b60-86b4-40d453312c46-9895940.PNG?alt=media\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 216px;\" />&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "4c541b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8684"}, {"id": "40f2c1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8685"}, {"id": "529be1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8686"}, {"id": "747484", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8687"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8688", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae6"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b59"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b29"], "question": {"text": "Three infinitely long charged thin sheets are placed as shown in figure. The magnitude of electric field at the point $P$ is $\\frac{x \\sigma}{\\epsilon_o}$. The value of $x$ is _______ (all quantities are measured in SI units).\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FZ47sHm9MBekJNh_U0cT9gbBvyiSmH-EoCdp_RPO4IuQ.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "2590de", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8689"}, {"id": "afbfbe", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a868a"}, {"id": "8e146a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a868b"}, {"id": "01338b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a868c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a868d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae6"], "topics": ["60ced3320e34b73944ddfaa5"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e4d"], "question": {"text": "The electric field in a region is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">E</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">0</mn></msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">E</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">0</mn></msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> The flux of this field through a rectangular surface, area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math> parallel to the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>Z</mi></math> plane is _______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "b0060e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a868e"}, {"id": "7d867b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a868f"}, {"id": "a2681c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8690"}, {"id": "9785f5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8691"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8692", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae6"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b59"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8ed5"], "question": {"text": "<p>Two small spheres each of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mg</mi></math> are suspended from a point by threads <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> long. They are equally charged and repel each other to a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The charge on each of&nbsp;the sphere is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>21</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> will be ___.[Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>]</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "88a8ca", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8693"}, {"id": "2b3325", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8694"}, {"id": "be16ab", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8695"}, {"id": "f01941", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8696"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8697", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae6"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b59"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b12"], "question": {"text": "Suppose a uniformly charged wall provides a uniform electric field of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> normally. A charged particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> being suspended through a silk thread of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and remain stayed at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math> from the wall. Then the charge on the particle will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo></math> ________ [use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>]"}, "options": [{"id": "fe596d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8698"}, {"id": "46abf4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a8699"}, {"id": "47f71c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a869a"}, {"id": "64cc93", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a869b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a869c", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae6"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b59"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b29"], "question": {"text": "<p>A thin metallic wire having cross sectional area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is used to make a ring of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. A positive charge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is uniformly distributed over the ring, while another positive charge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo> </mo><mi>pC</mi></math> is kept at the centre of the ring. The tension in the ring is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_______</mi><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>; provided that the ring does not get deformed (neglect the influence of gravity).</p><p>(Given, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></msup></math> SI units)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "ac89ae", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a869d"}, {"id": "c25bad", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a869e"}, {"id": "e5cbb5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a869f"}, {"id": "6f2c8d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a86a0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a86a1", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae6"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b59"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8ed5"], "question": {"text": "Two equal positive point charges are separated by a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></math>. The distance of a point from the centre of the line joining two charges on the equatorial line (perpendicular bisector) at which force experienced by a test charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> becomes maximum is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></mfrac></math>.&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is ______."}, "options": [{"id": "9950b2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a86a2"}, {"id": "2df551", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a86a3"}, {"id": "2a7d09", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a86a4"}, {"id": "13f2b4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a86a5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a86a6", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae6"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b59"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b12"], "question": {"text": "<p>A uniform electric field of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is created between two parallel charged plates (as shown in figure). An electron enters the field symmetrically between the plates with a kinetic energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The length of each plate is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>)</mo></math> of deviation of the path of electron as it comes out of the field is ______(in degree).</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fb0a2f662-96ce-4fec-af47-df9ffda86136-9894312.PNG?alt=media\" style=\"width: 327px; height: 160px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "3dd511", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a86a7"}, {"id": "0f27aa", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a86a8"}, {"id": "78571a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a86a9"}, {"id": "e49e4c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9c2ee0e063d92a86aa"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:30:52.305Z", "up